# Development & Changelog Workflow

**Goal:** Separate completed work from planned work. BACKLOG looks forward; CHANGELOG looks back. No staleness.

## The Three-Changelog System

RealmPal maintains three separate changelogs for three audiences:

### 1. BACKLOG.md (product roadmap - this is forward-looking)

**What goes here:**
- Current priorities and in-progress work
- Blocked items with root causes and unblock conditions
- Technical decisions already made
- Next items to start
- Research notes and findings

**What goes here after completion:**
- Nothing. Remove completed work and archive it to CHANGELOG.md

**Structure:**
- "Resume order when context is fresh" at top (next priorities)
- Blocked section (explain why, not just "waiting")
- Each active feature as a section with "**done**" marker when complete
- Do not edit BACKLOG the week after a feature ships (let CHANGELOG capture it)

### 2. CHANGELOG.md (developer changelog - technical & migrations)

**What goes here:**
- Every completed version (not every commit)
- Breaking changes, migrations, technical details
- Linked commits
- Internal refactors, tests, infrastructure
- Known issues and blockers at time of release

**What goes here when:**
- After a feature is **ready to deploy** (all tests pass, reviewed)
- When moving from BACKLOG to CHANGELOG, expand brief notes into full technical detail
- Add migration guides if the change affects operations

**Workflow:**
1. While building: keep notes in BACKLOG under "In Progress"
2. When done: create [YYYY.MM.DD] section in CHANGELOG.md with full technical writeup
3. Remove from BACKLOG (don't keep stale copies)
4. Add related user-visible items to web/lib/changelog.ts (see rule 3 below)

### 3. web/lib/changelog.ts (user-facing changelog - UI modal only)

**What goes here:**
- User-visible improvements only
- Short, benefit-focused, no jargon
- One sentence per bullet; 1-4 bullets per entry

**What goes here when:**
- Same release day as CHANGELOG.md (if there are user-visible changes in that release)
- See `.cursor/rules/changelog.mdc` for the full guide

**Note:** Internal refactors, performance work with no visible effect, added tests, etc. do NOT go here.

